<title>USA: USDA gross cutout hide and offal value.</title>
<headline>USDA gross cutout hide and offal value.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The hide and offal value from a typical slaughter steer for Friday was estimated at $9.58 per cwt live, down -0.03 when compared with Thursday's value.-USDA</p>
<p>FOB CENTRAL U.S., TODAY'S CALCULATIONS FOR BY-PRODUCT VALUE</p>
<p>(STEER) -			  Lbs    Price  Change    Value</p>
<p>Steer hide, butt brand	 5.39   84.50    -	 5.84</p>
<p>Tallow, edible		   1.20   25.25    -	 0.30</p>
<p>Tallow, packer bleachable    4.50   23.25   -0.50    1.05</p>
<p>Tongues, Swiss #1 Wht 0-3%   0.26  200.00    -	 0.52</p>
<p>Cheek meat, trmd		 0.32   65.00    -	 0.21</p>
<p>Head meat			  0.13   44.50    -	 0.06</p>
<p>Oxtail, selected		 0.16  131.00    -	 0.21</p>
<p>Hearts, reg, bone out	  0.38   25.00    -	 0.10</p>
<p>Lips, unscalded		  0.11   72.00    -	 0.08</p>
<p>Livers, slcted, gall off     0.96   35.00    -	 0.34</p>
<p>Tripe, scalded edible	  0.65   18.50    -	 0.12</p>
<p>Tripe, honeycomb bleached    0.15   50.00    -	 0.08</p>
<p>Lungs, inedible		  0.47    4.60    -	 0.02</p>
<p>Melts				0.14    6.25    -	 0.01</p>
<p>Meat bone ml, 50% blk/ton    3.70  256.50   -6.00    0.47</p>
<p>Blood meal, 85% blk/ton	0.60  575.00    -	 0.17</p>
<p>TOTAL :			   19.12			  9.58</p>
<p>The average value of hide and offal for the five days ending Friday, January 17, 1997 was estimated at 9.63 per cwt., down -0.01 from last week and up 1.46 from last year.</p>
